# Testing Standards

**Valid tests, not overmocked.** Behavior changes require automated tests before done.

## Rules

### Do

- Test happy path + at least one error/edge path
- Bug fixes: regression test that fails on parent commit
- Assert observable behavior — not implementation details
- Use factories/fixtures — no copy-pasted IDs across tests
- Run focused tests during dev; full suite before push

### Do not

- Mock the module under test for persistence logic
- `expect(true).toBe(true)` no-op tests
- Defer tests to "later sprint"
- Skip CI with `.skip` without documented reason

### Mocking allowed for

- External APIs (LLM, OAuth, third-party HTTP)
- Clock/time when testing scheduling
- Not for your own DB/ORM when testing service persistence

## Coverage target

≥ 90% on **new/changed** code paths. Full-repo coverage is aspirational; changed behavior must be locked by tests.

